From: Wave7 development <wave7-test@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: rtl8365mb: escalate persistent RTL8367D SerDes faults

The stock 067 firmware's RTL8367D DW8051 has an internal recovery
sequence in addition to link-state polling. Its exact instructions
were traced against a mock ASIC register bus. The sequence asserts
SDS 0x003f bit 5, pulses SDS 0x0400 bit 2, then clears bit 5.

Keep the existing first mode edge and fast link-down retries. For
persistent faults on the evidenced silicon revision, alternate the
known mode edge with the stock-derived internal pulse. Preserve
unrelated bits and serialize the full sequence under the indirect
window mutex. Track ambiguous assertion-write failures and retry
release in reverse order before another recovery attempt or PCS
configuration. Keep DW8051 disabled; no simultaneous register owners.

This is an experimental candidate. The stock sequence is observed
for link-down events; application to corrupt-only ingress is a
hypothesis, not a hardware-proven correction.

Signed-off-by: Wave7 development <wave7-test@localhost>
---
